00:01:32,209 --> 00:01:33,676
Show yourself !

10
00:01:48,292 --> 00:01:50,260
I know you 're out there .

11
00:02:11,148 --> 00:02:12,172
( exclaims )

12
00:02:17,354 --> 00:02:18,378
( ROARS )

13
00:02:20,023 --> 00:02:21,047
( GASPS )

14
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:27,655
Help !

15
00:02:28,065 --> 00:02:29,259
Help me !

16
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:30,423
( GRUNTlNG )

17
00:02:33,937 --> 00:02:35,529
Somebody help me !

18
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,132
Help !

19
00:03:01,331 --> 00:03:02,958
Alas ! Poor Yorick .

20
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:04,758
I knew him , Horatio .

21
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:09,770
A fellow of infinite jest , of most excellent fancy .

22
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,471
He hath borne me on his back a thousand times ,

23
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:16,636
and now , how abhorred in my imagination it is !

24
00:03:16,747 --> 00:03:18,612
My gorge rises at it .

25
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:22,347
Here hung those lips .. .

26
00:03:23,053 --> 00:03:24,543
( PEOPLE laughing )

27
00:03:34,431 --> 00:03:35,398
Excuse me .

28
00:03:35,499 --> 00:03:37,330
This is a private party , miss .

29
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:41,699
My name is Gwen Conliffe , and I 'm engaged to your brother , Ben .

30
00:03:42,739 --> 00:03:44,036
is Ben here ?

31
00:03:44,941 --> 00:03:45,908
No .

32
00:03:47,744 --> 00:03:51,703
I 'm afraid no one knows where Ben is , which is why I 'm here .

33
00:03:55,752 --> 00:03:56,946
Clive .

34
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:06,657
Well , boys and girls , let 's repair to the tavern !

35
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:16,237
Good night , sweet prince .

36
00:04:16,773 --> 00:04:19,799
I seem to recall , Miss Conliffe .. .

37
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:39,586
I seem to recall he mentioned you in one of his letters .

38
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:42,062
And it 's quite uncharacteristic of my brother

39
00:04:42,165 --> 00:04:44,190
to treat a lady in such a way ,

40
00:04:44,334 --> 00:04:48,430
but the character of man is such a shiftable thing .

41
00:04:48,572 --> 00:04:52,303
You misapprehend me . Benjamin is missing from Blackmoor .

42
00:04:52,409 --> 00:04:53,376
He 's gone .

43
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:56,440
Did my father send you ?

44
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,343
No , I 'm here on my own .

45
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:01,813
It 's been nearly a month since anyone has seen Ben ,

46
00:05:01,918 --> 00:05:04,182
and we knew that you were in London .

47
00:05:05,422 --> 00:05:07,913
I 'd hoped you had received some word .

48
00:05:08,024 --> 00:05:09,787
Why do you think he 's in trouble ?

49
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:14,227
Because the night he went missing , two villagers were killed .

50
00:05:15,365 --> 00:05:16,798
Would you help us ?

51
00:05:18,001 --> 00:05:19,662
Miss Conliffe ,

52
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:23,806
I am under contract for the next 30 performances .

53
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:27,874
If this is about your father , I know how you feel .

54
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:29,846
Do you ?

55
00:05:34,951 --> 00:05:37,613
My company leaves for America tomorrow .

56
00:05:38,488 --> 00:05:40,786
I simply can 't help .

57
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:43,654
He is your brother .

58
00:05:44,461 --> 00:05:45,826
Good night .

59
00:05:52,168 --> 00:05:53,897
It must be a wonderful luxury ,

60
00:05:54,004 --> 00:05:57,098
doing battle with imaginary demons , Mr. Talbot .

61
00:05:58,174 --> 00:06:00,404
Mine right now are very real .

62
00:06:58,134 --> 00:06:59,567
Your mother ?

63
00:07:05,208 --> 00:07:06,175
Yes .

64
00:07:07,243 --> 00:07:09,837
My oldest memories of my mother ,

65
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:13,141
we are gathering grapes in her father 's vineyard .

66
00:07:13,783 --> 00:07:15,910
It is my Garden of Eden .

67
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,485
You 're paying yours a visit ?

68
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:22,484
No , my mother died not long after this was made .

69
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:27,692
My father and my brother , they live near Blackmoor .

70
00:07:34,404 --> 00:07:36,929
A man needs a good stick on the moor .

71
00:07:38,108 --> 00:07:42,602
I purchased this one in Gévaudan lifetimes ago .

72
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:46,071
It 's the work of a master silversmith .

73
00:07:47,917 --> 00:07:49,680
Would you do me the honor ?

74
00:07:56,593 --> 00:07:57,890
It 's beautiful .

75
00:07:57,994 --> 00:07:59,689
It will give me great pleasure to know that

76
00:07:59,796 --> 00:08:02,822
it was the keeping of a civilized man .

77
00:08:03,366 --> 00:08:08,531
Its heft is somewhat too much for me these days .

78
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:11,407
You 're overly kind .

79
00:08:13,176 --> 00:08:15,576
But I 'm afraid I must refuse it .

80
00:08:16,846 --> 00:08:18,404
As you wish .

81
00:10:11,161 --> 00:10:14,528
( DOOR creaking )

82
00:10:25,426 --> 00:10:26,552
Hello ?

83
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,560
( birds twittering ) ( wings fluttering )

84
00:10:34,368 --> 00:10:36,199
( SNARLlNG )

85
00:10:36,303 --> 00:10:37,463
Samson !

86
00:10:47,915 --> 00:10:49,143
Lawrence ?

87
00:10:50,117 --> 00:10:51,584
Hello , Father .

88
00:10:52,019 --> 00:10:53,077
Ah .

89
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:57,681
Lo and behold , the prodigal son returns .

90
00:10:58,392 --> 00:11:00,121
I hope you 're not expecting the fatted calf .

91
00:11:00,227 --> 00:11:01,216
( SAMSON GROWLS )

92
00:11:01,328 --> 00:11:02,386
Stay !

93
00:11:04,865 --> 00:11:06,423
We don 't have many visitors .

94
00:11:06,533 --> 00:11:08,000
You seem well .

95
00:11:08,135 --> 00:11:10,126
I 've often wondered what you look like .

96
00:11:14,108 --> 00:11:15,575
You 've come about your brother , have you ?

97
00:11:16,276 --> 00:11:17,334
Stay .

98
00:11:18,045 --> 00:11:19,103
Yes .

99
00:11:19,413 --> 00:11:21,381
Miss Conliffe learned that I was in London .. .

100
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:22,504
( SAMSON continues growling )

101
00:11:22,616 --> 00:11:23,583
Samson .

102
00:11:23,684 --> 00:11:24,810
... and sent me a letter

103
00:11:25,619 --> 00:11:28,087
saying that Ben has disappeared .

104
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:30,281
I thought I 'd offer my help in any which way I can .

105
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:33,014
Yes , what a splendid idea , Lawrence .

106
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,351
A splendid idea .

107
00:11:34,428 --> 00:11:36,293
Too late , I 'm afraid .

108
00:11:36,396 --> 00:11:38,193
Unfortunately , your brother 's body

109
00:11:38,298 --> 00:11:42,530
was found in a ditch by the priory road yesterday morning .

110
00:11:42,936 --> 00:11:45,461
I assume you have something to wear for the funeral .

111
00:11:45,572 --> 00:11:49,099
Sir John . You remember my son , Lawrence ?

112
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:51,537
Singh , my servant .

113
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,438
Master Lawrence .

114
00:11:54,915 --> 00:11:57,179
It 's nice to see you , Lawrence .

115
00:11:58,051 --> 00:11:59,848
It 's good that you 're here .

116
00:11:59,953 --> 00:12:01,477
Has Miss Conliffe been notified ?

117
00:12:01,588 --> 00:12:02,646
Mmm-hmm .

118
00:12:03,257 --> 00:12:05,885
She 's upstairs in her bedroom , asleep .

119
00:12:06,026 --> 00:12:10,224
( piano playing )

120
00:12:14,601 --> 00:12:16,660
Where are they keeping Ben 's body ?

121
00:12:51,471 --> 00:12:54,565
Your father instructed me to bury your brother 's effects with him .

122
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:56,700
It seems a shame .

123
00:12:58,545 --> 00:12:59,842
Thank you .

124
00:13:01,381 --> 00:13:03,474
I wouldn 't , sir. lt 's .. .

125
00:13:04,818 --> 00:13:06,752
I missed his whole life .

126
00:13:37,517 --> 00:13:39,644
( PEOPLE laughing )

127
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:45,750
MONTFORD : What if it wasn 't a beast at all , but a cunning murderer ?

128
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,751
Someone who bore a grudge against one of these men .

129
00:13:48,862 --> 00:13:51,797
To misdirect the authorities , he kills the men ,

130
00:13:51,899 --> 00:13:53,389
and then he tears up the bodies

131
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,627
to make it look like a wild beast was responsible .

132
00:13:55,736 --> 00:13:57,931
Ridiculous ! Who would go to such lengths ?

133
00:13:58,038 --> 00:13:59,516
What about that gypsy dancing bear ?

134
00:13:59,542 --> 00:14:00,554
It could have done it .

135
00:14:00,641 --> 00:14:02,734
( SCOFFS ) That mangy thing ?

136
00:14:03,477 --> 00:14:05,536
Kill three men ? I doubt it .

137
00:14:05,812 --> 00:14:08,246
I saw the bodies with my own eyes .

138
00:14:09,049 --> 00:14:10,682
Unnatural wounds .

139
00:14:10,708 --> 00:14:12,339
Most unnatural .

140
00:14:12,953 --> 00:14:14,944
Made by a fell creature , I say .

141
00:14:15,055 --> 00:14:17,046
Damn gypsies wandering the countryside ,

142
00:14:17,157 --> 00:14:19,387
bringing their woe and deviltry with them .

143
00:14:19,493 --> 00:14:22,326
They show up , and two weeks later this happens !

144
00:14:22,429 --> 00:14:25,364
My guess is Ben Talbot went to their camp

145
00:14:25,465 --> 00:14:27,433
to have it off with a gypsy whore .

146
00:14:27,868 --> 00:14:29,028
The bear gets hold of him ,

147
00:14:29,136 --> 00:14:30,967
and they dump what 's left of him in the ditch !

148
00:14:31,071 --> 00:14:32,766
Got nothing to do with the gypsies .

149
00:14:35,066 --> 00:14:37,057
Twenty-five years ago now ,

150
00:14:37,769 --> 00:14:39,327
me Pa found him .

151
00:14:39,804 --> 00:14:42,034
Quinn Noddy and all his flock .

152
00:14:42,140 --> 00:14:45,234
Brains and guts and God-knows-what

153
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:47,868
lying all over the moor for a quarter mile .

154
00:14:48,246 --> 00:14:50,578
And , Quinn , the look on his face .

155
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:54,242
Like he 'd been eaten alive .

156
00:14:55,486 --> 00:15:00,014
Whatever did it was big , had claws ,

157
00:15:00,124 --> 00:15:02,217
and didn 't mind a load of buckshot .

158
00:15:02,994 --> 00:15:05,926
After that , me Pa went home and ..

159
00:15:05,952 --> 00:15:09,356
.. melted down me Ma 's wedding spoons

160
00:15:10,301 --> 00:15:12,599
and cast silver bullets on them .

161
00:15:14,839 --> 00:15:19,833
Wouldn 't leave the house on a full moon from then on .

162
00:15:27,585 --> 00:15:30,884
He thought it was a werewolf .

163
00:15:34,292 --> 00:15:35,725
I still say that bear 's to blame .

164
00:15:36,294 --> 00:15:38,694
You 'd think the Talbots would 've learned their lesson , eh ?

165
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:40,895
Consorting with the Romas .

166
00:15:40,999 --> 00:15:44,093
Right . Remember that black-eyed Salome the old man married ?

167
00:15:44,202 --> 00:15:47,069
Went crazy up there in the ward , killed herself .

168
00:15:47,171 --> 00:15:50,470
She was a gypo whore queen or some such , wasn 't she ?

169
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:51,542
LAWRENCE : Yes .

170
00:15:52,143 --> 00:15:53,610
She was crazy

171
00:16:00,151 --> 00:16:02,881
for coming to this shithole you call a town .

172
00:16:03,288 --> 00:16:04,482
What did he say ?

173
00:16:04,989 --> 00:16:07,514
You 're in your drink , boy .

174
00:16:10,995 --> 00:16:13,395
Get him out of my tavern , Nye !

175
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:15,399
Come on , lad .

176
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,797
If you want to do something about it ,

177
00:16:16,901 --> 00:16:18,300
I 'll be outside .

178
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:21,564
My mother wasn 't a whore .

179
00:16:28,346 --> 00:16:30,246
Lawrence Talbot ?

180
00:16:37,588 --> 00:16:39,385
( indistinct chattering )

181
00:16:47,365 --> 00:16:48,627
Good evening .

182
00:16:48,733 --> 00:16:51,600
Please join us. lt 's good to see you up and about .

183
00:16:53,237 --> 00:16:56,206
Refreshed , recovered and as enchanting as ever .

184
00:16:56,808 --> 00:16:58,139
Please , join us .

185
00:17:01,446 --> 00:17:03,004
Good evening , Miss Conliffe .

186
00:17:03,114 --> 00:17:04,138
Good evening .

187
00:17:05,950 --> 00:17:07,941
What a pleasant surprise .

188
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:12,714
May I recommend the baked eel ?

189
00:17:13,491 --> 00:17:16,517
Singh has outdone himself this evening , haven 't you , Singh ?

190
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:20,893
Something plainer .

191
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:21,987
Thank you .

192
00:17:24,402 --> 00:17:27,565
I was a moment ago telling my son

193
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:31,039
that the telegraph system does reach us here in lonely old Blackmoor .

194
00:17:33,244 --> 00:17:36,407
Do you find your home much changed , Mr. Talbot ?

195
00:17:39,150 --> 00:17:42,085
Blackmoor does seem rather the same as I left it .

196
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:43,719
How so ?

197
00:17:44,255 --> 00:17:48,055
The villagers , they still have the same wild ideas .

198
00:17:48,159 --> 00:17:52,220
Yes , well , they 're a provincial lot , I must say ,

199
00:17:53,064 --> 00:17:56,033
ignorant and superstitious to a worldly man such as yourself .

200
00:17:56,134 --> 00:17:58,932
We 're savages at the ends of the earth .

201
00:18:00,805 --> 00:18:02,739
I didn 't intend to start a squabble .

202
00:18:03,107 --> 00:18:08,636
All I 'm saying is that you dismiss the natural man at your peril .

203
00:18:08,746 --> 00:18:09,713
That 's all .

204
00:18:09,814 --> 00:18:12,977
I find your insecurities quite strange , Father .

205
00:18:13,184 --> 00:18:16,711
No , you mistake that for my self-awareness .

206
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:19,823
And how comfortable are you in your skin , may I ask ?

207
00:18:20,024 --> 00:18:23,187
One can get used to anything .

208
00:18:23,294 --> 00:18:24,283
Excuse me .

209
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:44,275
You know , Lawrence , I 've never understood what it is that you do ,

210
00:18:44,382 --> 00:18:46,543
pretending to be other people .

211
00:18:46,784 --> 00:18:50,117
But I understand you 're highly celebrated and famous for it .

212
00:18:50,455 --> 00:18:53,447
Perhaps one day I 'll see for myself what all the fuss is about .

213
00:18:53,558 --> 00:18:55,617
I think your mother would 've liked that .

214
00:18:55,726 --> 00:18:58,354
She loved you and your brother with all her heart .

215
00:18:58,529 --> 00:19:00,326
Why did she do it ?

216
00:19:03,401 --> 00:19:05,767
She struggled with life , as we all do .

217
00:19:08,206 --> 00:19:09,673
She lost .

218
00:19:10,208 --> 00:19:11,869
Does that answer your question ?

219
00:19:12,577 --> 00:19:14,704
I saw Ben 's body today .

220
00:19:15,246 --> 00:19:17,714
What kind of animal could have done such a thing ?

221
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:21,141
I 've seen the work of a Kodiak bear and a Bengal tiger ,

222
00:19:21,385 --> 00:19:23,853
nature at its most vicious ,

223
00:19:24,055 --> 00:19:26,580
but I must say , I 've never seen anything like this .

224
00:19:28,426 --> 00:19:30,951
People in town say it was a man .

225
00:19:31,095 --> 00:19:32,221
( CHUCKLES )

226
00:19:33,865 --> 00:19:36,493
You mean a raving lunatic at loose on the moor ?

227
00:19:36,767 --> 00:19:40,032
Yes , it 's possible , but I think I would have run him down with my dogs .

228
00:19:41,072 --> 00:19:43,165
On the other hand ,

229
00:19:43,741 --> 00:19:46,539
the wounds are so terrible that only something human

230
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:49,545
would seem capable of such wanton malevolence .

231
00:19:50,214 --> 00:19:53,149
I found a strange medallion among Ben 's belongings .

232
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,028
Yes , Saint Columbanus .

233
00:19:56,054 --> 00:19:58,272
He was an Eastern saint .

234
00:19:58,623 --> 00:20:00,386
He was also a gypsy .

235
00:20:01,192 --> 00:20:03,854
So did Ben have dealings with the gypsies ?

236
00:20:06,364 --> 00:20:10,733
Yes , he was our negotiator .

237
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,064
The local gentry would pay a fee ,

238
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,867
and the gypsies would keep their criminal activities to a minimum .

239
00:20:17,742 --> 00:20:23,237
And they would move on once they 'd sold the local lads all the wine

240
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:26,077
and dark-haired ladies they could stand .

241
00:20:34,125 --> 00:20:38,585
" That orbèd maiden with white fire laden , Whom mortals call the moon ,

242
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:42,063
" Glides glimmering o 'er my fleece-like floor .. . ' '

243
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:46,135
" By the midnight breezes strewn . ' '

244
00:20:48,573 --> 00:20:51,474
She exerts enormous power , doesn 't she ?

245
00:20:57,114 --> 00:20:59,173
I wish things were different .

246
00:20:59,817 --> 00:21:03,218
Never look back , Lawrence . Never look back .

247
00:21:03,487 --> 00:21:05,955
The past is a wilderness of horrors .

248
00:21:11,862 --> 00:21:16,390
Lawrence , I 'm glad you 're home .

249
00:21:30,014 --> 00:21:31,140
( SOFT knocking ON DOOR )

250
00:21:33,284 --> 00:21:34,581
Can I help you , sir ?

251
00:21:34,685 --> 00:21:37,711
I was hoping to have a word with Miss Conliffe .

252
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:39,784
Just a moment , sir .

253
00:21:41,659 --> 00:21:42,683
( DOOR opening )

254
00:21:56,007 --> 00:21:57,474
Miss Conliffe .

255
00:21:57,908 --> 00:22:00,001
My behavior was unacceptable .

256
00:22:03,347 --> 00:22:04,939
These were Ben 's .

257
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,508
He 'd want you to have them .

258
00:22:13,624 --> 00:22:17,822
If there 's anything you need , anything at all , please let me know .

259
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:23,289
I want to know what happened to him .

260
00:22:25,369 --> 00:22:27,337
I 'll do everything I can .

261
00:22:27,605 --> 00:22:28,902
Thank you .

262
00:22:33,110 --> 00:22:34,873
Thank you for coming .

263
00:22:55,266 --> 00:22:58,258
( children whispering )

264
00:23:15,808 --> 00:23:18,276
( children giggling )

265
